    "id": "unified-example-directed-relationship",
    "name": "Slow-burn directed relationship pacing",
    "description": "Confirm a new considerate interaction, stamp accepted story time, apply small authored directed deltas with scene/day caps, cooldown and diminishing returns, and persist the private projection after Apply.\n\nSetup: Create actor-private JSON mara-relationship for actor character:mara.png as {values:[{key:\"mara-to-elias-attraction\",value:18,subjectId:\"character:mara.png\",objectId:\"character:elias.png\"},{key:\"mara-to-elias-desire\",value:6,subjectId:\"character:mara.png\",objectId:\"character:elias.png\"}],ledger:[]}. Create public JSON story-clock with the actual accepted timeline. Select Mara as the native active character. Set Entities to the real canonical IDs. Bind Prose and decision. Attraction/desire are portrayal state; neither grants consent or compels an action. This recipe updates Mara's directed feelings only; build a separately scoped leg for Elias.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
